{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397965,"nonce":"NtCPAWUB/vieRqVwk1NS2wiA1AQ=","title":"LSP diagnostics: only type-check errors, published against the wrong file","message":"`LspContext::compile_file` (`lsp/src/context.rs:59`) runs `lower_to_tast` with analysis skipped.\n- Errors found later (MIR lowering, safety analysis, macro failures reported downstream) never reach the editor. `emit_safety_warnings` is false.\n- Every error is published to the buffer being edited, even when its location is in another file.\n- `code` is always the string \"rayzor\" instead of the error code (E0100...).\n- `suggestion` is appended to the message text instead of becoming a code action.\n- Related errors are dropped (`related` is collected and never sent as `relatedInformation`).\n- Only the edited buffer is compiled from memory. Other open, unsaved buffers are read from disk, so cross-file errors are stale.\n- A parse failure is reported at 0:0 as \"Parse: ...\".\n- Diagnostics are published without the document version.\n\nSee f646d327a479d3130d6464acc42bf8a61d028dd752d60354c7e61e7725c5eb10 for spans.","files":null}]}